  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas exists in a state with pressure $P_0$ volume $\\mathrm{V}_0$.It is isothermally expanded to 4 times of its initial volume $\\left(\\mathrm{V}_0\\right)$, then isobarically compressed to its original volume. Finally the system is heated isochorically to bring it to its initial state. The amount of heat exchanged in this process is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GHwxj",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{~V}_0(2 \\ln 2-0.75)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "VaxEd",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{~V}_0(\\ln 2-0.75)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wP6gE",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{~V}_0(\\ln 2-0.25)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ttgji",
      "text": "$P_0 V_0(2 \\ln 2-0.25)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/rbb3JpnqJ0LtZIcUiwPULzDiFzpxHYbMbm338lcPV-s.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\omega_1=P_0 v_0 \\ln 4 \\\\ & \\omega_2=\\frac{P_0}{4}\\left(-3 v_0\\right)=-\\frac{3 P_0 v_0}{4}\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\omega_3=0 \\\\ & \\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{\\text {cyclic }}+\\omega\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\omega \\quad\\left(\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{\\text {cyclic }}=0\\right)$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{v}_0\\left(\\ln 4-\\frac{3}{4}\\right) \\\\ & =\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{v}_0(2 \\ln 2-0.75)\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
